<img src="ritual1.jpg" alt="Magic Ritual">

<p id=Extract>It has come to my attention that many metaphysically-oriented persons are organizing to cast
a &quot;binding spell&quot; on the man currently illegally occupying the White House. The problem is, the
spells I've seen include elements of outrage, which not only weaken the spell&mdash;they can strengthen
the person at whom the spell is cast, which is obviously the opposite of what is desired.</p>

<p>To explain to future readers what the heck this is about, I must first be sure you've heard that 
<a href="http://time.com/4433880/donald-trump-ties-to-russia/" target="_blank">Russian interference</a> 
with our national election in November, 2016, plus other factors such as 
<a href="http://billmoyers.com/story/real-way-2016-election-rigged/" target="_blank">gerrymandering</a>, 
<a href="http://www.zerohedge.com/news/2016-11-22/scientists-find-persuasive-evidence-vote-hacking-demand-clinton-recount-3-states" target="_blank">hacked 
voting machines</a>, and a
<a href="http://thepoliticalinsider.com/dnc-rigged-stole-election-from-bernie-sanders/">corrupt Democratic National Convention</a> 
that ignored the will of its constituents, put a man into the White House who didn't win the popular vote and who, in fact,
has demonstrated a desire to walk back our democracy 150 years. (In 2017, his supporters, who seem unable to
grasp any reality that conficts with the pretender's lies, don't believe any of the evidence, which they
refuse to even examine. But the reality will be clear enough to future readers.)</p>

<p>Given this interloper's horrifying and treasonous actions since he took over, and the increasing number of people showing up
at almost daily protests against him, it should be no surprise that virtual groups around the world are also gathering to 
<a href="https://www.meetup.com/pro/resist/" target="_blank">#Resist</a>; and some of those groups include Wiccans, witches, 
magicians, wizards, New Agers, and the like. And many of <i>those</i> groups have planned to hold 
simultaneous <i>binding spells</i> tonight, and at each repeat of the waning 
crescent moon, until the imposter has been removed from office. In fact, the instructions have been 
<a href="https://extranewsfeed.com/a-spell-to-bind-donald-trump-and-all-those-who-abet-him-february-24th-mass-ritual-51f3d94f62f4#.18cnyg5iv" target="_blank">published 
on the Internet</a>.</p>

<p>A binding spell is <i>not</i> a hex or a curse. Rather, it is a spell intended to prevent its target from hurting
himself or others. Essentially, just as you can put a shield of protection around yourself (by envisioning yourself
surrounded by a shield of White Light), you can put that shield around someone else who is so dangerous (or insane) that
he or she poses a threat to others. It doesn't harm them, but does prevent them from performing further harmful actions.</p>

<p>The thing is, it's very important when performing a ritual like this, that one <i>not</i> hold thoughts of harm against
the one at whom the spell is cast. If the spell is performed in a state of anger or fear, it will have the <i>opposite</i> of
the desired effect.</p>

<p>Rather, you must maintain the attitude you would have as you gently explained to an acting-out 5-year-old why he must sit
in the corner for awhile. &mdash;That is, a feeling of <i>love and kindliness</i> for the target. If you have trouble feeling
love for him, try feeling love for his victims (currently, immigrants, Muslims, Native Americans, and transgendered children,
but we'll soon all be affected if he isn't stopped). But remember, he, like you and I, is a part of All That Is and has merely
lost his way, as so many of us do on occasion. <b>The real purpose of a binding spell isn't punishment,
but rather protection for the target from himself.</b></p>

<p>With all that in mind, I am hereby offering a gentler (and, I think, more effective) binding spell.</p>

<hr />

<p>This spell is to be cast at midnight EST (the time zone the pretender most often occupies, whether in the White House,
his tower in New York, or his vacation property in Mar-a-Lago, Florida. There's nothing magic about the time,
other than that the simultaneity of thousands of magicians casting the spell at the same time should make it more effective. The
date of the first casting is tonight, the night of the waning crescent moon; with subsequent castings monthly for as long as the pretender 
illegally occupies the top seat of our government: March 26th; April 24th; May 23rd; June 21st (especially important as it is the summer solstice); 
July 21st; August 19th; etc.</p>

<h3>Components</h3>

<p>Gather these items together so you have them when you need them (midnight EST, which is 10 PM in Phoenix).</p>

